<title>UK: ICO coffee exports up at 6.87 mln bags in January.</title>
<headline>ICO coffee exports up at 6.87 mln bags in January.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>International Coffee Organisation (ICO) exporting members exports rose to 6.87 million 60-kg bags in January from 6.34 million in December and 6.12 million in January 1996, ICO figures showed on Wednesday.</p>
<p>In the 12 months to January 1997 total exports rose to 76.38 million bags from 67.88 million in the same 1996 period.</p>
<p>In the first four months of the current 1996/97 coffee year to January total exports were up at 26.22 million from 23.64 million in the same 1995/96 period.</p>
<p>Latest ICO export data, in thousand bags, included --</p>
<p>		     Jan 97    Jan 96   Oct/Jan 96/97  Oct/Jan 95/96</p>
<p>    Brazil	 1,428	 787	 7,199	    4,026</p>
<p>    Colombia	 976	 782	 4,136	    4,120</p>
<p>    Guatemala	334	 368	 1,280	    1,048</p>
<p>    Mexico	   871	 745	 1,745	    1,565</p>
<p>    Indonesia	182	 265	 1,592	    1,670</p>
<p>    Uganda	   551	 552	 1,842	    1,402</p>
<p>    Vietnam	  682	 569	 2,006	    1,834</p>
<p>    Ivory Coast    103	  70	   299		479</p>
<p>-- Jalil Hamid, London newsroom +44 171 542 4985</p>
